Key Points to Remember
• 401 vs 403: 401 = not authenticated (no or wrong credentials); 403 = authenticated but the role is not
allowed. USER calling an ADMIN endpoint gets 403.
• hasRole('ADMIN') automatically checks the authority ROLE_ADMIN. Do not write ROLE_ inside
hasRole(); use hasAuthority('ROLE_ADMIN') if you want the full name.
• @EnableMethodSecurity (Spring Security 6) replaces the older @EnableGlobalMethodSecurity and
turns on @PreAuthorize. It works through Spring proxies, so it applies to methods of Spring beans
called from outside.
• Alternative (URL-based): .requestMatchers("/api/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN") inside
the SecurityFilterChain gives the same result without annotations.
• Store roles without the ROLE_ prefix (ADMIN, USER); .roles() adds it.
• H2 in-memory: the seeded users and items are recreated on every restart.
